onument Records from 1968 to 1971.  This marks the first album appearance of Stevens' novelty hit single \"Bridget the Midget (The Queen of the Blues).\"  This collection contains two more singles from Barnaby while the rest are recordings for Monument (five singles and three album tracks). \" Gitarzan\" is the album version that begins with noises of an audience.  \"Harry the Hairy Ape\" and \"Ahab the Arab\" are not the original recordings but re-recordings that were made for Monument.  \"Mr. Businessman\" is the album version.]\n\n[[Monument Records] Monument Records was an American record label in Washington, D.C. named for the Washington Monument, founded in 1958 by Fred Foster and Buddy Deane (a prominent Baltimore disc jockey at WTTG).  Buddy Deane soon left the company, and in the early 60's bought KOTN in Pine Bluff, Arkansas where he retired until his death.  Foster relocated to the Nashville suburb of Hendersonville, Tennessee.  Monument's releases include a variety of genres, including rock and roll, country, jazz, and rhythm and blues.]\n\nQuestion: Which American singer-songwriter known as \"the Caruso of Rock\", recorded on the Monument Records label and had hits such as \"Pretty One,\" and \"Uptown\"?","terminal_format_issue":"Format Agent is not selected as the Output Agent","topology_statistics":{"agent_count":0,"component_count":0,"directed_edge_count":0,"fan_in_agent_ids":[],"fan_out_agent_ids":[],"max_depth":0,"max_width":0,"output_agent_id":null,"quotient_directed_edge_count":0,"reciprocal_pair_count":0,"relation_count":0,"root_agent_ids":[],"root_component_count":0,"sink_agent_ids":[],"sink_component_count":0,"structural_depth":0,"topology_family":"empty","topology_motifs":[]}}","role":"user"},{"content":"{
